            <ArticleTitle>Cutaneous Mycobacterium gordonae infection in an elderly diabetic returned traveller.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1093/jtm/tax019</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Mycobacterium gordonae, a low pathogenicity organism, is rarely implicated in skin and soft tissue infections. We present a 77-year-old returned diabetic traveler from rural Sudan with cutaneous M. gordonae infection. Several months of ciprofloxacin, rifampin and ethambutol led to resolution of his plaque, without signs of recurrence at 6-month follow-up.</AbstractText>
